    title: "Coverage narrowing is opt-out and narrows the merge-CI manifest"  # 10ee
    status: todo_hard  # 10ee
    priority: 2  # 10ee
    parent:  # 10ee
    tags:  # 10ee
    - smart_test  # 10ee
    - ci  # 10ee
    isbefore: []  # 10ee
    duplicate_of: []  # 10ee
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 10ee
    pr_ref:  # 10ee
    description: "Owner ruling 2026-11-12 (reverses the 11-11 opt-in ruling): coverage-directed narrowing is OPT-OUT.\n\n- smart-test narrows by default (coverage-select narrow); --no-narrow turns it off for a run.\n- Narrowing moves ABOVE the manifest seam, so the committed .ci/affected-tests.txt (what merge CI runs) is narrowed by default, and the manifest header says how many tests narrowing removed.\n- The Woodpecker full-suite cron is never narrowed (full-suite.yml does not read the manifest).\n\nAcceptance: a change whose narrow drops tests produces a manifest without them and a header line saying so; --no-narrow restores the unnarrowed manifest; tests pinning the old split (test_smart_test_manifest_split.py and kin) state the new contract.\nHazards to handle: a stale index can drop a test covering part of a changed file (the local scoped-coverage gate runs the same set first); CI checks coverage per package with only that package's manifest tests."  # 10ee
    fields: {}  # 10ee
- op: discuss  # 1de6
  at: '2026-11-13T04:03:42Z'  # 1de6
  by: agent  # 1de6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1de6
  clock: 2  # 1de6
  nonce: 1de6  # 1de6
  message: "Pre-build measurement (2026-11-12): applying coverage-select narrow's own refusal rules (selection_index.narrowing_blockers) to the last 200 origin/dev commits that change packages/*/src/*.py, with comment/docstring-only files excluded as smart-test excludes them: 163 (81.5%) would REFUSE because an import-time block (module or class body) changed, 5 (2.5%) add or delete a file (also refuse), 32 (16.0%) are narrowable. Ignoring docstring-only differences in import-time blocks moves only 10 commits: 76.5% refuse, 21.0% narrowable. A refusal leaves the run set unchanged, so default-on narrowing would act on about 1 source-changing commit in 6, and even then only on the ~55% of wall-clock the index can speak about (measure-narrowing-headroom). Script: job tmp refusal_rate2.py. Reported to the owner before building."  # 1de6
